{"id": "EUVD-2026-97717", "enisaUuid": "386c4cd4-dd02-3175-aa97-6f76cc6ea8ba", "description": "ImageMagick before 6.9.13-57 and 7.x before 7.1.2-32 contains an information disclosure vulnerability in the PostScript decoder, which allocates a buffer one byte longer than the data it decoded. Attackers can supply a crafted PostScript file to expose a single uninitialized byte of memory contents.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T15:35:17", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-5j8x-vq8c-vrp9", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/5a5c2e51948fcc5d85b8d832938e2c1b4db4a699", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/a32215ba7a193f2bc896ba6ed4be4013cc06e22b", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-before-6.9.13-57-and-7-x-before-7.1.2-32-information-disclosure-in-postscript-decoder"], "aliases": ["GHSA-m3mr-78pc-g3jj", "CVE-2026-109273"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.31, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0665a40a-fdfa-31a5-9f1d-74b3b8e52b8f", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0-0 <7.1.2-32"}, {"id": "0a950ef8-5811-33c8-a1ca-578356739fcc", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.9.13-57"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1c7334c1-cbf7-3d0c-b584-4c70fa0b12f1", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}